{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Consent"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A report of each drop of held or recovered records, in the order they happen."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dropReports"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AsyncQueue","identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8Trackers17ConsentDropReportO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ConsentDropReport","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/ConsentDropReport"},{"kind":"text","text":"> { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reports wait until they are read. A record dropped for room is reported as it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dropped; while that report waits unread, later ones merge into it, one report counting","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them all across their timestamps. So the reports waiting unread hold at most one overflow","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"report between any two others (denials and finished trackers), however many events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"overflow. The sequence ends once the consent is gone and every report has been read.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One task reads the reports at a time. The first iterator to read holds them until its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iteration ends or it is released; a second reader meanwhile waits its turn, logging a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"warning once, then reads on from the next report, so the first gets every report in order."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A reader cancelled while it waits returns "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Consent\/dropReports"},"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Consent.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Trackers\/Consent.swift#L117"},"title":"dropReports","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"Trackers"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:8Trackers7ConsentV11dropReports11AsyncQueues0E5QueueVyAA0B10DropReportOGvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV","text":"AsyncQueue","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8Trackers17ConsentDropReportO","text":"ConsentDropReport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/trackers\/consent\/dropreports"]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers/Consent":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Consent","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trackers\/consent","title":"Consent","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Consent","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The user’s consent, category by category, which a tracker given it applies to every event."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Consent"},"doc://AsyncQueues/documentation/AsyncQueues/AsyncQueue":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AsyncQueue"}],"title":"AsyncQueue","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/asyncqueues\/asyncqueue","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AsyncQueue"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Elements in the order they are enqueued, kept until they are read; one reader at a time reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}]},"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers/ConsentDropReport":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ConsentDropReport","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trackers\/consentdropreport","title":"ConsentDropReport","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConsentDropReport","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Records a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Consent","type":"reference"},{"text":" dropped before they were delivered, and why.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/ConsentDropReport"},"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers/Consent/dropReports":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trackers\/consent\/dropreports","title":"dropReports","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncQueue","preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConsentDropReport","preciseIdentifier":"s:8Trackers17ConsentDropReportO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A report of each drop of held or recovered records, in the order they happen."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"